# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# On Colab the notebooks read the SAME .env as part one, from Drive:
#   /content/drive/MyDrive/sar-transfer/.env
# (env.load_env looks there first; the Colab server cannot see your local disk.)
#
# Use short-lived, least-privilege tokens: a file on Google Drive is readable by
# anything that has access to that Drive.

# huggingface.co -> Settings -> Access Tokens. A read token is enough for the
# gated model weights (DINOv3, C-RADIOv4) and for reading your private converted-data
# repos back. Notebooks 02 and 03 load only this key; if it cannot read those repos,
# they copy the data from Drive instead.
HF_TOKEN=

# huggingface.co -> Settings -> Access Tokens. A write token, only for uploading
# the CONVERTED datasets to your private repos <account>/sar-transfer-<dataset> (with '-' for '_':
# glacial-lakes, snow, forty-v1, glavitu-alp; the account is set in the notebooks).
# Read only by notebook 01's upload cell (env.secret), never put into the environment.
HF_WRITE_TOKEN=
